From 2a23016ad16f363559566a27b4ad3915f430d658 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:25:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: the level 5 block describes what is drawn
 over the bars

ETSI GS CCM 001 V1.1.1, 6.2.2: the level 5 offsets "specify the active
area of current picture, in terms of a rectangular region specified in
picture coordinates", and the metadata of levels 1 and 2 "shall be
applied to the active area". Where Kodi draws its GUI or subtitles over
the bars of a film, the picture transported has pixels outside the
film's area, and the display was still told the film's: it may leave
them out of its mapping, or blank them (two other Dolby Vision forks
report menus clipped in the bars, and send zero offsets while the GUI is
visible).

Now, in both transports, the level 5 block sent with a frame is the
film's active area taken out to what is drawn over it: on each edge of
the active picture beyond which something is drawn, the offset sent is
0, the bars of that edge taken into the area. The area then holds every
pixel of the picture and of what is drawn over it, and black of the
bars, as the film's own does. The smallest rectangle around what is
drawn would need its bounds on the CPU before the packets are made; an
edge each gives one of 16 areas, which dvbridge_candidate_cover() makes
again once the edges are known (the candidate keeps a copy of the
metadata and the serializer's state before it). The blanking margins
stay the film's. Where the area sent changes because of what is drawn
(it is taken out, comes back, or goes out to other edges), the frame
refreshes the scene (scene_refresh_flag "indicates that the picture,
which DM metadata affects, is the first picture of a scene"), so that
the display starts its mapping again on the area the metadata now
applies to; the metadata id changes with the payload as always. Frames
whose area is the film's, after frames whose area was the film's, are as
before.

- What is drawn is known by the alpha of the picture of the composed way,
  now 2 in the converted transport as well (its bars and its clear too),
  and by the GUI composite's alpha factors, a + dst (1 - a), in both:
  2 stays where nothing is drawn. The colour is blended and packed as
  before; what captures read of the alpha is clamped to 1.
- The edges are measured on the GPU (dvbridge_source_cover()): a point
  for each pixel of the bars lands, where something was drawn over it, on
  the single pixel of a 1x1 target with the edges it lies beyond as its
  colour, blended by their maximum; the CPU reads it back. It waits for
  the GPU there, which it does anyway in the way that waits; where frames
  are presented a frame ahead it does not, and every edge that has bars
  is taken instead (the area is then the whole raster on those edges,
  still all that is in the picture).
- The window system marks a frame drawn over where the GUI is composited
  onto the picture or PQ subtitles are drawn into it, and asks the packing
  accordingly (CDVBridgeGLES::Pack(), Cover).
- The check of the bytes (dvverify) checks frames without GUI elements:
  its reference is packed with nothing drawn over it, the film's area, as
  the frame it checks; its candidate is prepared from the frame's
  transport state, so the scene refresh of the first frame after the GUI
  left the bars is the reference's too. The warm-up packs its composed
  picture with what is over the bars measured, so that the program of
  the measurement is ready before the GUI first appears.
- The Dolby Vision page of the player information shows the area sent
  with what is drawn over the bars on a row of its own, "L5 sent (with
  what is over the bars)" (Estuary #32005, and its Spanish).

Measured on Mesa's software OpenGL ES (zink on lavapipe), not on a GPU or
a display, with the test of the source transport on the integrated tree and the
libplacebo of the LibreELEC tree with 9932, on a picture of a profile 7
FEL stream with bars (offsets 0 0 275 276):
- the level 5 block sent, frame by frame, in a sequence of nine frames in
  each transport (nothing drawn over, twice; the GUI over the bars,
  twice; something inside the active picture only; nothing; drawn over
  with every edge that has bars taken, as a frame ahead does; nothing,
  twice): in all 18 frames the area, the scene refresh flag and the
  metadata id are those that the rectangles the test drew give, and the
  packets' CRCs are right; the edges measured on the GPU are those that
  the alpha of the picture read back gives (6 frames), and those are the
  rectangles' (8 frames);
- 6 mutations each make it fail: the top edge counted as the bottom one,
  only an alpha below 1 counted as drawn over, the area not taken out,
  no scene refresh where the area sent changes, an alpha of 1 for the
  picture of the converted transport (found because what the test
  expects comes from the rectangles it drew, not from that alpha), and
  the edges measured where the GPU is not to be waited for;
- where nothing is drawn over the bars, the frames are as before: with the
  pictures converted, the render test of the bridge gives
  the hashes of before it in every drawing (230 lines; the float picture's
  alpha is now 2, so the copy of the test this is measured with hashes
  and checks the range of its colour only, as that render test
  has to); in the source transport, the 176 drawings of the test of the
  previous commit, every byte that of the test's reference and every DM
  header right;
- the check of the bytes (20 checks, identical) and the warm-up (no
  program compiled after it) with this commit: as given in the previous
  one.
What only the display can tell: whether the LG C5 blanks, or leaves
unmapped, what is drawn over the bars with the film's area, and whether
the scene refresh when the GUI comes and goes into the bars shows.

On top of "windowing/gbm: tell of a held mode change with the commit
that makes it": the frame that makes a held change of mode is not
presented a frame ahead (CHeldModeAnnouncement), also where its
presentation is asked early to choose how the level 5 block is taken
out: it waits for the GPU, so its block is measured.
